  {
    "slide": 7,
    "text": [
      "Traits are determined by specific ",
      "genes",
      ", or segments of DNA",
      ". Different variations of genes are known as ",
      "alleles",
      ". In most cases, one allele is ",
      "dominant ",
      "over the other, influencing the way such genes are expressed…",
      "The ",
      "dominant ",
      "allele (represented by capital letter) is ",
      "always expressed when present",
      "A ",
      "recessive ",
      "allele (represented by ",
      "lowercase",
      " letter) is only ",
      "expressed in the absence of the dominant allele. ",
      "The allele that encodes brown eyes ",
      "(B)",
      ", for example, is dominant over the recessive allele that encodes blue eyes (b). ",
      "GENES, ALLELES AND TRAITS"
    ],
    "images": [
      {
        "relationshipId": "rId3",
        "archiveMember": "ppt/media/image1.jpg",
        "file": "sources/slide-assets/slide-7-image1.jpg",
        "bytes": 76801,
        "sha256": "508ee6c2de2a4d74eb2a976214737298c960c8fb1dd519ffd66cc2c00cb5260f",
        "pixelReviewStatus": "not yet reviewed in this batch"
      },
      {
        "relationshipId": "rId4",
        "archiveMember": "ppt/media/image26.jpg",
        "file": "sources/slide-assets/slide-7-image26.jpg",
        "bytes": 29896,
        "sha256": "006a1c500e99dd602aa6b8adc16438e7fedf3e9f947ae2c2dd890ee9dcb6c1b4",
        "pixelReviewStatus": "not yet reviewed in this batch"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "slide": 8,
    "text": [
      "",
      "This means that although we receive genes from both parents, our characteristics are ",
      "NOT",
      " determined by the “blending” of our parents traits",
      ". It is determined by the dominant vs. recessive interaction of the alleles we ",
      "receive.",
      " ",
      "Phenotype",
      " refers to the ",
      "outward expressio",
      "n of traits. For example, having brown eyes or having blue eyes.",
      "Genotype",
      " on the other hand refers to the ",
      "combination of alleles",
      " an individual has for a given trait. ",
      "For example, your teacher’s ",
      "genotype for eye color is ‘bb’",
      ". Since she only has recessive alleles, this means that her ",
      "phenotype is ‘having blue eyes’",
      "",
      "PHENOTYPE VS. GENOTYPE",
      "",
      "Note: A phenotype isn’t always a visible trait like color. It could be a behaviour or a physiological trait, such as ‘able to digest lactose’ or ‘not able to digest lactose. "
    ],
    "images": []
  },
  {
    "slide": 9,
    "text": [
      "This child’s dad donated an allele encoding brown eyes (B). Her mom donated an allele encoding blue eyes (",
      "b)",
      ". Because the “brown eye” allele or “B” is dominant to the “blue eye” allele or “b”, her eyes appear brown rather than blue. ",
      "Another ",
      "Example:"
