  {
    "slide": 26,
    "text": [
      "Because of the Law of Segregation, as long as the ",
      "mode of inheritance",
      " of a particular trait and the genotypes of two parents are known, we can use a Punnett Square to determine the possible genotypes of offspring.",
      "Autosomal dominant mode of inheritance",
      " = trait is dominant & inherited on an autosome (as opposed to the sex chromosomes)",
      "",
      "Autosomal recessive mode of inheritance",
      " = trait is recessive & inherited on an autosome (as opposed to the sex chromosomes) ",
      "MODE OF INHERITANCE"
    ],
    "images": []
  },
  {
    "slide": 27,
    "text": [
      "Example",
      ":",
      "In mice, black fur is inherited in an ",
      "autosomal domina",
      "nt",
      " ",
      "manner (black fur is ",
      "dominant to brown fur).",
      ".. ",
      "",
      "List the genotypes of a black mouse and a brown mouse.",
      " ",
      "If a heterozygous black mouse is crossed with a brown mouse, what is the probability that their offspring will have black fur? Brown fur? ",
      "Single Trait",
      " Crosses",
      "Possible genotypes for a ",
      "black",
      " mouse: BB or Bb",
      "Possible genotype of a brown mouse: bb",
      "",
      "",
      "?",
      "The probability of having black fur is 2/4 = ",
      "1/2",
      "  or 0.50.",
      "",
      "The probability of having brown fur is  also 2/4 = 1/2  or 0.50.",
      "",
